# Directory manifest for an IW4 x64 (IW4MS) fastfile project.
#
# Each line is a class and a path, separated by a tab. The tree under
# templates/fastfile/ is generated from this file, and
# templates/buildfile asserts that every directory in it carries a
# README.md.
#
# The set of directories was taken from a complete Unlinker dump of the
# retail IW4x x64 zone tree, being 116 zones in each of four languages,
# and was then checked against the OAT loader and dumper sources.
# Directories that exist in retail but hold content rather than
# structure, such as the per weapon subdirectories of sound/weapons/,
# are deliberately omitted.
#
# The class determines whether the directory name belongs in a zone
# definition:
#
#   asset   The directory name is supplied by the tooling. The zone
#           definition names the asset on its own, or gives a path below
#           the directory, but does not repeat the directory itself. For
#           example, "fx,muzzleflashes/pistolflash" is built from
#           fx/muzzleflashes/pistolflash.efx.
#
#   raw     The asset name is the path itself. The entry repeats this
#           directory and includes the extension, as in
#           "rawfile,animscripts/dog/dog_combat.gsc".
#
#   sub     The directory does not appear in a zone definition. Its
#           files are written by the dumper of another asset and are
#           referred to by name from within that asset.
#
# Keep the entries sorted within each class.
#
asset	zone_source
asset	english
asset	english/localizedstrings
asset	images
asset	materials
asset	materials/fonts
asset	materials/gfx
asset	materials/gfx/icons
